{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: make \"bootstrap with a policy\" the default construction of a room. Today R-GEN-10 step 6 seals the initial policy-activated event from main at import or from the R-POL-7 default, and the R-POL-7 default has no owners and no require rules. Hugh's direction (2026-10-02): every room is founded with an explicit policy document, and the default is the GitHub-like starter pack from docs/policy-pack.md (owner review, claim before propose, required checks, admin approval for policy changes), with the founding admin's team as the fallback owner for every path. A founder may choose another pack or an explicit none, and an import whose main already has .artroom/policy.json keeps it. Decide and record how the chosen pack reaches main: for a new repository as part of the initial commit; for an import without a policy, state whether founding commits the pack on main (the room is the only writer of main, R-PUB-1) or activates it as the initial policy without a commit, and why. The genesis or entry 1 must name the pack and its digest so the choice is auditable. Contract amendment in docs/protocol.md (R-GEN-10, R-POL-7, R-POL-9), the policy package (a named default pack and a compile step at founding), lane A (founding), lane E (CLI and MCP founding options), docs/policy-pack.md, and the demo repository. Start after lane A's current amendment-3 follow-up lands.","body":{"conditions":"(1) docs/protocol.md amended so that founding records an explicit policy choice: a named pack with its digest, or none, and the initial policy-activated event names it; R-POL-7 becomes the behaviour of the explicit none choice only. (2) packages/policy exports the default pack with a fallback owner parameter, and founding compiles it. (3) Lane A: RoomDraft and Founding carry the policy choice; a new repository's initial commit contains .artroom/policy.json; an import without a policy file follows the recorded decision; an import with one keeps it. (4) Lane E: artroom founding on CLI and MCP defaults to the pack and offers the other choices. (5) docs/policy-pack.md and the demo repository show the default founding. (6) Tests for each path and the acceptance cases cited by rule number; root gates pass.","target_head":"72d6abde5c6dfa993ac441884e8f966a903b932f","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}